course: dictionary
lesson: 4349
title: Guilty: a feeling or a verdict
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: "Guilty" has three main meanings. The first is a feeling: you feel bad because you know you did something wrong. «Kyle felt shocked, then guilty for being so cross» shows a feeling inside a person.
explain: The second meaning is about having done something wrong or against the law. «Faking an injury to avoid a race lets your team down and leaves you feeling guilty» links the wrong thing with the bad feeling that follows it.
explain: The third meaning is a legal one. A court decides whether someone is guilty or not guilty. «A jury is twelve ordinary adults picked at random who listen to a criminal trial» and then they make that decision.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. Ask: is this about a feeling, or a decision made in a court? Then swap in "feeling bad about a wrong" and check it still makes sense.
fact: Guilty is an adjective. Its other forms are guiltier and guiltiest.
fact: «Feel guilty» means to feel bad because you know you did something wrong.
fact: «Guilty of» means you have done the thing named, as in «guilty of lying».
fact: «Found guilty» means a court has decided you broke the law.
fact: «A guilty conscience» is a bad feeling inside that tells you something needs putting right.
exercise: «Kyle felt shocked, then guilty for being so cross.» What does guilty mean here? | Very tired after a long day | Found by a court to have broken the law | Happy and proud | *Feeling bad because he knew he had done something wrong
exercise: «A jury ... decide whether the person is guilty or not guilty.» What is the jury deciding? | Who will win the race | Whether the person is tall | *Whether the person broke the law | Where the trial will be held
exercise: «He sat and watched, bored and guilty, while his team ran one runner short.» Find and copy the word that shows a feeling of having done wrong. | runner | *guilty | watched | team
test: Which phrase means a court has decided someone broke the law? | Feel guilty | Guilty conscience | *Found guilty
test: Ravi says a guilty conscience means he has to go to court. What does it really mean? | *A bad feeling inside that shows something needs putting right | A tired feeling after a long walk | A happy feeling after a game | A court trial with a jury
exam: Which sentence shows guilty as a feeling? | «Dev's mum told Kyle's mum that Dev's dad had moved out.» | «A jury is twelve ordinary adults picked at random.» | *«Faking an injury to avoid a race leaves you feeling guilty.»
